 "discussion": {
  "office": "SLC",
  "issued": "2026-11-18T04:45:00+00:00",
  "key_messages": "- Winter Weather Advisories remain in effect for the Wasatch and western Uinta Mountains, along with the Wasatch Back, where additional accumulating snow is expected. - Another storm system will bring significant mountain snow Thursday into Friday, with snow levels falling near to below 5000 feet by Friday. Another 6 to 12 inches of mountain snow, with locally higher amounts near 2 feet for the upper Cottonwoods is expected in northern Utah, while 4 to 10 inches of mountain snow is forecast for central and southern Utah. - Freezing temperatures are increasing in probability for the Virgin River corridor near Zion National Park Saturday and Sunday mornings.",
  "synopsis": null,
  "short_term": null,
  "long_term": null,
  "url": "https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=SLC&issuedby=SLC&product=AFD"
 },
